      vlan) _describe 'action' '('locate:Find one or many VLANs from one or many roots. Depth zero inspects roots; positive depth traverses LLDP/CDP-confirmed switch links breadth-first.' 'propagation:Build a root-by-VLAN propagation matrix, traversing every reachable switch layer within the depth/node bounds.' 'set:Guarded VLAN change wrapper. Requires --dry-run or --confirm. --file runs a batch, one independent <target> <interface> --access|--trunk <vlan> [--native N] [--replace] change per line; --skip-unverified excludes lines that dont resolve or arent approved instead of aborting the whole batch.')' ;;
      lookup) _describe 'action' '('core:Run core lookup and cache observations into memory.' 'mac:Inspect local evidence, search forwarding tables, profile an edge port, show movement history, or query cached authoritative IEEE MA-L/MA-M/MA-S assignments.' 'mac-online:Resolve the longest matching IEEE MA-L, MA-M, or MA-S assignment with organization details, cache time, and source provenance.' 'mac-registry:Inspect or refresh the private cache of all three IEEE public MAC assignment registries.' 'mac-all:Search every online switchs forwarding table for a MAC and report where it is attached. Each switch along the path lists the MAC, so hits on known uplink ports are shown separately as transit and the remaining hit is the access port the device is on. Run netrune topology stp first so uplinks are known, and ping the address first so the switches have learned it.' 'mac-inspect:Correlate cached identity, L2 location, IP, vendor, inventory, and movement evidence without touching devices.' 'mac-locate:Search switch forwarding tables directly, independent of whether the endpoint has an IP address.' 'mac-profile:Locate a MAC, then gather best-effort interface, LLDP/CDP, PoE, device-tracking, OUI, and core ARP evidence at likely edge ports.' 'mac-history:Show newest-first MAC location and identity events.' 'mac-vendor:Resolve the locally installed OUI prefix. This identifies an organization, not an exact model.')' ;;
