ort each AP is on. Runs: netrune ap neighbors (SSH, seconds).' 'ap-moves:APs that changed switch or port, newest first. Runs: netrune ap moves (none, instant).' 'ap-history:Where one AP has been attached over time. Runs: netrune ap timeline <ap> (none, instant).' 'ap-unjoined:APs the controller lists as not joined. Runs: netrune ap unjoined (none, instant).' 'ap-refresh:Re-read APs from the controllers and switches. Runs: netrune ap scan (SNMP, minutes).' 'find:Find a switch or AP by any part of its name, IP, MAC, serial, or model. Runs: netrune inventory list (none, instant).' 'find-mac:Live: which switch port a MAC is on now (access port, not the uplinks it crosses). Runs: netrune lookup mac all <mac> (SSH, seconds).' 'find-ip:Ask the core switchs ARP/MAC tables who an IP or MAC is. Runs: netrune lookup core <ip|mac> (SSH, seconds).' 'mac-history:Every port and identity a MAC has had, newest first. Runs: netrune lookup mac history <mac> (none, instant).' 'ip-history:Who has held an IP over time. Runs: netrune memory ip <ip> (none, instant).' 'port-history:What has been plugged into one switch port over time. Runs: netrune memory port <switch> <port> (none, instant).' 'vlan-where:Live: where a VLAN exists, starting from a switch. Runs: netrune vlan locate <switch> <vlan> (SSH, seconds).' 'vlan-trace:Live: follow a VLAN switch by switch from a root and show where it stops. Runs: netrune vlan propagation <switch> <vlan> (SSH, minutes).' 'path:The L2/L3 path to an endpoint on a VLAN, hop by hop, with findings. Runs: netrune path inspect <endpoint> --vlan <vlan> (SSH, seconds).' 'port-health:Live: speed/duplex negotiation and error-counter growth on one port. Runs: netrune diagnose port-health <switch> on <port> (SSH, seconds).' 'cable:The last recorded cable (TDR) result for a port; starts no test. Runs: netrune diagnose cable <switch> on <port> (none, instant).' 'latency:Round-trip time, jitter, and loss to a target. Runs: netrune diagnose latency <target> (ping, seconds).' 'internet:Is the Internet reachable and unfiltered: DNS, TLS, and filtering checks. Runs: netrune diagnose filtering google.com (Internet, seconds).' 'speed:This machines Internet speed. Runs: netrune diagnose speed (Internet, minutes).' 'device:Everything Netrune knows about one device: identity, history, relationships. Runs: netrune memory device <name|ip> (none, instant).' 'same:Are these two records the same switch? Evidence and conflicts. Runs: netrune device identity <device> <device> (none, instant).' 'support:Manufacturer, model, driver, and what Netrune can safely do on it. Runs: netrune device support <device> (none, instant).' 'merges:Manual device merges in force. Runs: netrune inventory merges (none, instant).' 'hardware:Live: re-read model, Motherboard serial, and base MAC over SSH. Runs: netrune device inventory (SSH, seconds).' 'db:Quick database health: storage, references, labels, identities, merges, caches, stuck jobs. Runs: netrune db coherence (none, seconds).' 'db-fix:The same, and fix what has one right answer (re-apply merges, relabel, drop switches filed as APs). Runs: netrune db coherence --realign (none, seconds).' 'db-deep:Full SQLite integrity check (slower). Runs: netrune db integrity (none, seconds).' 'db-size:Where the database is, its size, schema, and record counts. Runs: netrune db status (none, instant).' 'backups:Backup history for a device. Runs: netrune backup history <device> (none, instant).' 'config-diff:What changed between a devices last two different configs. Runs: netrune backup diff <device> (none, instant).' 'backup-all:Back up every online device whose config changed. Runs: netrune backup run --all --skip-recent (SSH, minutes).' 'doctor:Is this machine set up right: tools, routes, trust, core settings. Runs: netrune diagnose doctor (none, seconds).' 'vault:Is the SSH vault locked or open, and until when. Runs: netrune vault status (none, instant).')' ;;
      init) _describe 'action' '('run:Create neutral XDG profile state and report required and optional system tools.')' ;;
      profile) _describe 'action' '('list:List profiles and show which one is active.' 'show:Show one profiles paths and effective non-secret settings.' 'create:Create a neutral, private profile without changing the active profile.' 'use:Select the profile used by future commands.' 'paths:Show the active profiles XDG-owned directories.' 'export:Write the active profile to one file for another machine: its configuration (controllers, filters, subnets, aliases, channels, drivers, SSH known_hosts) and flat caches; --with-state adds the SQLite memory and configuration backups; --with-secrets adds the SNMP communities and encrypts the whole file with a passphrase (from NETRUNE_BUNDLE_PASSPHRASE, or asked). The SSH vault and named secrets are bound to this machine and never exported.' 'pack:Everything a new machine needs, in one encrypted file: the same as profile export FILE --with-state --with-secrets (configuration, caches, memory, SNMP communities). Guarded because it carries credentials: without --confirm it lists what would go in; --confirm asks for a passphrase (or NETRUNE_BUNDLE_PASSPHRASE), writes the file, and records an audit event. Restore with ./install.sh --import FILE or netrune profile import FILE.' 'import:Restore a bundle written by profile export into its profile (or --as NAME) and make it active. Refuses a profile that already holds configuration or memory unless --force, which keeps each replaced file beside the new one. An encrypted bundle asks for its passphrase (or NETRUNE_BUNDLE_PASSPHRASE). Prints what is left to do: netrune vault set for the SSH password.' 'migrate-legacy:Copy legacy netsnmp state into a private profile, recording a manifest and leaving originals untouched.')' ;;
